   247	## Reusable knowledge
   248	
   249	- The contract has one server-managed HttpOnly `openclaw_session`, `absoluteLifetimeSeconds: 28800`, and `rememberMe: false`. Phase-one "saved login state" therefore means only the current browser's valid server session; do not use `localStorage`, `sessionStorage`, or `document.cookie` for persistent or multi-account state. [Task 1]
   250	- P1 must remain visible and require an explicit card choice even when a cookie exists. P2 then checks the selected mode: personal requires `personal_web/internal`; organization requires `organization_lark/lark` with active membership, workspace, and Feishu binding. [Task 1]
   251	- A matching session may show masked identity and a deliberate continue action. Missing, expired, revoked, or mismatched sessions fall back to password login or, only when needed, Feishu OAuth/QR, without account or tenant enumeration. [Task 1]
   252	- Keep the strict `/openclaw/media/api/session` response unchanged. The proposed read-only phase-one surface is `GET /openclaw/auth/entry-state?mode=personal|organization`; any future activation/switch mutation must preserve same-origin checks, `X-OpenClaw-CSRF`, and appropriate session rotation. [Task 1]
   253	- Relevant authority and checks: `openclaw-bot-center/contracts/media_web_business_pages.openapi.yaml`, `openclaw-bot-center/contracts/media-auth-route-contract.json`, `openclaw-tag-router/openclaw_app/adapters/http_api.py`, `openclaw-tag-router/openclaw_app/account/workspace_resolution.py`, `npm run qa:media-login-contract`, and `npm run build:media`. [Task 1]
